      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Beyond just the tutorial resources benefit: I think the Slack was once acceptable for a lot of cultural benefit that forums could provide because of the existence of conversation threads, allowing for more detailed, deeper engagement with the community. Without that kind of structure I and many others rarely find it rewarding to participate in the chat at all, and as a result feel much more cut off from the community than before.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
